# TypeScript Standards

- Use TypeScript strictly; avoid `any` unless unavoidable and briefly justified.
- Prefer explicit domain types in `*.types.ts`; keep DTOs/schemas close to the module/feature.
- Validate external input with Zod at boundaries (API handlers, forms). Infer types from schemas when practical.
- Prefer `async/await` over raw promise chains; never swallow errors in empty `catch`.
- Name files by role: `*.routes.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `*.repository.ts`, `*.schema.ts`, `*.types.ts` (backend); feature folders on clients.
- Do not commit secrets, tokens, or `.env` values into source.
